<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Maze Navigation Game.</span> As shown in Table <a href="#S5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 5 Experiment ‣ EvoEmpirBench: Dynamic Spatial Reasoning with Agent-ExpVer" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, applying <span id="S5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Agent-ExpVer</span> to both open-source and proprietary models boosts their Maze Navigation performance by an average of <math id="S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,+5.6\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5.6</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,+5.6\%</annotation></semantics></math> in success rate and <math id="S5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,+9.5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>9.5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,+9.5\%</annotation></semantics></math> in mean score. In particular, <span id="S5.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GPT-4.1</span> achieves a <math id="S5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,+5.56\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5.56</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,+5.56\%</annotation></semantics></math> (absolute) / <math id="S5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,+7.6\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>7.6</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,+7.6\%</annotation></semantics></math> (relative) increase in success and a <math id="S5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,+243.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>243.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,+243.3</annotation></semantics></math>–point / <math id="S5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,+9.5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>9.5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,+9.5\%</annotation></semantics></math> rise in score, making it the closest to human-level performance. Among open-source models, <span id="S5.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen-32B-instruct</span> with Agent-ExpVer posts <math id="S5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,+12.22\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>12.22</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,+12.22\%</annotation></semantics></math> / <math id="S5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,+28.96\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>28.96</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,+28.96\%</annotation></semantics></math> success and <math id="S5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,+410.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>410.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,+410.1</annotation></semantics></math>–point / <math id="S5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,+36.6\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>36.6</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,+36.6\%</annotation></semantics></math> score gains, surpassing nearly all peers and rivaling Deepseek-V3 and Qwen-30B-A3B.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The comprehensive metrics in EvoEmpirBench effectively evaluate model reasoning capabilities in complex environments. Our analysis reveals that stronger models achieve higher completion rates with fewer steps, while maintaining greater residual health points and demonstrating superior performance in coin collection, monster elimination, and obstacle destruction. These metrics collectively assess spatial reasoning in dynamic environments, risk-reward optimization, long-term versus short-term reward trade-offs, and interactive proficiency with virtual ecosystems.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span><span id="S5.T5.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">“All Levels” Metrics Across Models — Match-2 Elimination Game Performance.</span>
Top-3 values (exclude the
human baseline) in each category are highlighted in <span id="S5.T5.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFD700;">gold</span>, <span id="S5.T5.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#C0C0C0;">silver</span>, and <span id="S5.T5.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#CD7F32;">bronze</span>.
Metric abbreviations: Suc.Rate (Success Rate), A.Score (Avg. Score), R/M.S (Redundant/Missing Steps), Score/Step (Score per Step), Clear/Step (Clearance per Step), API Eff. (API Efficienc)</figcaption>
<p id="S5.T5.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.T5.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="font-size:70%;width:345.0pt;">
